WEBVTT

00:06.339 --> 00:08.341
[upbeat jazz]

00:20.520 --> 00:23.023
Hey, this isn't tight enough.

00:23.690 --> 00:25.775
- Right. Sorry about that.
- And look there.

00:25.859 --> 00:28.236
That jack's in the wrong position, man.
[grunts]

00:28.945 --> 00:30.447
Someone could get hurt.

00:31.406 --> 00:33.033
I already explained this to you.

00:33.867 --> 00:36.036
Why can't you do anything right, huh?

00:36.119 --> 00:37.245
I'm sorry.

00:37.912 --> 00:39.164
SUMIRE
PUFFERFISH CUISINE

00:39.247 --> 00:42.584
[Tatta] Kato keeps riding my ass
like I'm a stupid newbie.

00:44.335 --> 00:46.921
I can't work every day of the week
with no time off.

00:47.005 --> 00:49.549
I'm not like my dad.
He died from working too much.

00:51.384 --> 00:53.470
I'm doing this now,
but once I get enough money,

00:53.553 --> 00:55.180
I'm gonna take some courses,

00:55.263 --> 00:56.765
and I'll quit that dump.

00:56.848 --> 00:58.558
Then I'll do something really worthwhile.

00:58.641 --> 01:00.143
I'm sorry you feel like that.

01:02.979 --> 01:05.607
I plan to keep on
working hard at that dump.

01:06.524 --> 01:07.776
I like it there.

01:08.526 --> 01:10.070
Oh. I didn't…

01:10.153 --> 01:13.114
[man] Kato keeps riding you
because you have a bad attitude.

01:14.699 --> 01:17.077
You might learn to do the job right
before shitting on it.

01:17.994 --> 01:20.455
Sure, it might not be
the most exciting job,

01:20.538 --> 01:24.125
but I work my ass off every single day,
get my paycheck,

01:24.709 --> 01:26.461
and go home to my grateful family.

01:28.213 --> 01:30.465
Has anyone ever
been grateful to you for anything?

01:36.888 --> 01:37.972
[grunts]

01:38.556 --> 01:39.849
Hurry up now.

01:39.933 --> 01:41.935
- Move it.
- [grunts] Yes, sir.

01:42.018 --> 01:44.687
I'll take off the splash shield.
You remove the jack.

01:45.188 --> 01:46.189
Yes, sir.

02:04.791 --> 02:06.918
[Kato screaming]

02:07.001 --> 02:07.919
Get him out!

02:08.002 --> 02:09.963
- Hey, move! Get the car up!
- [Kato yelling]

02:10.046 --> 02:11.381
- Okay, go!
- Get it up!

02:11.464 --> 02:12.465
Get it up!

02:12.549 --> 02:14.092
- A whole turn!
- Hang on, Kato!

02:14.175 --> 02:16.427
- It's up! Hang on, almost there.
- Okay!

02:16.511 --> 02:18.096
- It's up. It's up.
- Kato, you okay?

02:18.179 --> 02:19.389
- Move it. Move!
- Come on.

02:19.472 --> 02:20.598
- Easy. Easy…
- Okay.

02:20.682 --> 02:21.683
- Get him out.
- Come on.

02:21.766 --> 02:23.977
- [yelling]
- Easy.

02:24.060 --> 02:25.270
- [Kato wailing]
- You're okay.

02:25.353 --> 02:26.312
- It's okay.
- Ugh!

02:26.396 --> 02:28.815
- Don't stand there! Call an ambulance!
- Are you all right?

02:28.898 --> 02:30.066
- Are you okay?
- Kato!

02:30.150 --> 02:31.442
- Kato!
- Look at his arm!

02:31.526 --> 02:32.902
- [gasping]
- [Kato wailing]

02:32.986 --> 02:34.320
The jack slipped!

02:35.155 --> 02:36.614
- Kato, hey!
- Hang in there, man!

02:36.698 --> 02:38.700
Hold it! Easy. Easy. Don't try to get up.

02:38.783 --> 02:40.451
[man] Kato decided to quit.

02:42.078 --> 02:43.037
[Tatta] Why?

02:43.955 --> 02:46.082
What do you think? He has no choice.

02:47.333 --> 02:49.627
His hand is completely useless now.

02:52.964 --> 02:55.091
You should leave. Get out!

02:59.888 --> 03:01.055
[machinery whirring]

03:01.139 --> 03:02.807
- [man 1] Thank you.
- [man 2] There it is.

03:03.391 --> 03:05.476
- Yeah.
- [man 3] Guys, break out those shocks.

03:05.560 --> 03:06.644
- You know the ones?
- Anyway…

03:06.728 --> 03:10.815
- I don't know when he's coming back.
- Do you know, uh… if he's coming back?

03:18.281 --> 03:20.491
- It kind of slipped out, man.
- Yeah.

03:20.992 --> 03:22.744
That Tatta is an idiot.

03:23.328 --> 03:25.288
I don't know. I don't know if…

03:28.458 --> 03:31.169
- …they rushed him to the hospital…
- He's all right…

03:35.006 --> 03:37.008
[gasping]

04:09.332 --> 04:11.334
[theme music]

05:11.853 --> 05:14.230
- [PA chimes]
- [computer] Nine minutes remain.

05:14.314 --> 05:17.525
The King of Clubs team is leading
by 500 points.

05:25.825 --> 05:27.035
[chuckles]

05:44.719 --> 05:46.763
- [Arisu] Aah! You bastard!
- [yells]

05:46.846 --> 05:49.682
[Arisu]
What the fuck are you doing? [roars]

05:49.766 --> 05:51.976
I just wanted to have a little fun
with your girlfriend

05:52.060 --> 05:53.394
before this stupid game was over!

05:54.520 --> 05:55.855
You asshole!

05:57.482 --> 05:59.525
Sure, you act like a hero.

06:00.109 --> 06:02.153
But I know you're just like me!

06:02.236 --> 06:05.073
I fucking hate how you walk around
like you're full of hope.

06:05.656 --> 06:08.701
Except now I can finally see
that hope draining out of you.

06:08.785 --> 06:11.371
And I'll die happy
knowing how pathetic you are.

06:12.830 --> 06:14.415
- [screams]
- [grunts]

06:14.499 --> 06:16.459
- [laughs]
- [Arisu yelling]

06:21.547 --> 06:23.049
- [laughs]
- [yells]

06:26.511 --> 06:27.470
[Maki sighs]

06:28.221 --> 06:29.555
[Maki] Eight minutes left.

06:30.973 --> 06:32.934
Seems like the enemy is laying low.

06:33.893 --> 06:36.521
[sighs] It's over, I guess.

06:37.605 --> 06:40.358
[sighs] What a letdown, huh?

06:40.441 --> 06:41.943
That's just how the game goes.

06:42.026 --> 06:44.237
There's no time left
for them to do anything.

06:47.031 --> 06:48.741
I think I'm gonna take a walk.

07:11.013 --> 07:12.765
This feels like an eternity.

07:13.891 --> 07:16.060
Just waiting here to die.

07:34.078 --> 07:36.956
[Usagi] Arisu. I'm sorry.

07:37.039 --> 07:38.749
I couldn't fight.

07:40.042 --> 07:41.878
I couldn't help you in the end.

07:42.462 --> 07:43.463
Usagi,

07:44.255 --> 07:45.798
I should apologize to you.

07:46.799 --> 07:47.925
I'm sorry.

08:07.778 --> 08:08.946
[Usagi] I'm sure

08:10.156 --> 08:12.325
if we went back, I'd still hate it there.

08:12.408 --> 08:14.285
No, staying here won't change that.

08:14.368 --> 08:15.703
- Usagi--
- [gasps]

08:17.330 --> 08:20.166
You can't push people
into following you for no reason.

08:21.167 --> 08:22.585
You have to be ready to listen.

08:23.544 --> 08:25.129
Wait for them to come to you.

08:27.423 --> 08:30.426
- [PA chimes]
- [computer] Seven minutes remain.

08:40.228 --> 08:41.979
[echoing clang]

08:44.273 --> 08:46.275
[wind whistling]

08:49.445 --> 08:51.447
[metal creaking]

08:55.409 --> 08:56.786
You decided to come.

08:59.622 --> 09:03.167
Something told me
that I would see you here.

09:07.880 --> 09:09.799
Something told me the same thing.

09:12.260 --> 09:13.553
That's why I came.

09:14.720 --> 09:17.098
To see if you might be
waiting for me here.

09:20.935 --> 09:22.186
The ocean is wide.

09:24.230 --> 09:25.856
That's why we're drawn to it.

09:26.732 --> 09:29.360
We want to commune
with something bigger than we are.

09:40.204 --> 09:41.914
[Arisu] Your team beat ours.

09:47.169 --> 09:48.921
[Kyuma] So do you have any regrets?

09:51.757 --> 09:52.925
To be honest,

09:54.677 --> 09:56.554
I'm a bit disappointed.

09:57.805 --> 10:01.017
- [PA chimes]
- Five minutes remain.

10:04.270 --> 10:06.022
[Arisu] Please, tell me, Kyuma.

10:10.067 --> 10:11.777
I need to know the answer.

10:13.404 --> 10:14.697
Before I die.

10:16.365 --> 10:17.950
[Kyuma] You know that I can't.

10:19.619 --> 10:20.786
You've given up.

10:24.749 --> 10:26.417
[Arisu] I thought you'd say that.

10:33.466 --> 10:34.634
Well, then…

10:36.761 --> 10:38.137
what about

10:39.347 --> 10:41.474
one last handshake

10:42.475 --> 10:43.684
before I go?

10:45.603 --> 10:47.063
What would you say to that?

10:48.356 --> 10:49.523
Handshake?

10:50.274 --> 10:51.859
The game isn't over yet.

10:52.860 --> 10:54.445
If we shake hands now,

10:54.945 --> 10:56.947
we would have to battle, and I'd win.

11:02.995 --> 11:05.331
I finally realized something about myself,

11:08.292 --> 11:09.627
because of what you said.

11:12.296 --> 11:13.923
I should have been ready to listen.

11:16.217 --> 11:18.386
I should have waited
for them to come to me.

11:19.970 --> 11:21.972
Let them know they could depend on me.

11:25.017 --> 11:26.769
And maybe we could've

11:27.269 --> 11:29.480
understood each other
a little better then.

11:32.900 --> 11:33.901
[sighs]

11:36.487 --> 11:37.947
I know we're enemies.

11:41.575 --> 11:43.035
You're my opponent.

11:46.622 --> 11:49.458
And I know it might seem
like I'm being crazy.

11:54.380 --> 11:56.549
But I still really want to say thank you.

11:59.385 --> 12:01.679
Thank you for helping me
realize those things.

12:07.727 --> 12:12.314
I know that… I don't have much time left
to do anything else.

12:15.568 --> 12:17.027
I know I'm gonna die.

12:19.029 --> 12:20.448
So please,

12:23.325 --> 12:25.327
let me shake the hand of the one…

12:26.829 --> 12:29.039
[sighs] …who showed me my true self.

12:41.010 --> 12:42.261
[sighs]

12:44.513 --> 12:45.347
All right.

12:46.849 --> 12:49.059
Since it's my opponent's dying wish,

12:49.935 --> 12:51.645
I'd be honored to grant it to you.

12:54.732 --> 12:57.443
Thank you, Kyuma.

12:59.320 --> 13:00.321
Arisu.

13:01.906 --> 13:03.491
Getting to battle with you

13:04.617 --> 13:05.951
was a great pleasure.

13:16.504 --> 13:18.464
[PA chimes]

13:19.048 --> 13:21.801
[computer] The scores have been updated.

13:22.384 --> 13:23.219
[gasps]

13:24.011 --> 13:24.887
[gasps]

13:25.471 --> 13:26.639
Uh… huh?

13:27.223 --> 13:28.307
Huh?

13:32.394 --> 13:33.687
Is this for real?

13:35.147 --> 13:38.150
[computer] The player team is leading
by 500 points.

13:38.234 --> 13:41.028
KYUMA: 14,000 LOSE
ARISU & TATTA: 14,950 WIN

13:45.991 --> 13:47.159
What?

13:48.285 --> 13:50.704
14,950 points?

13:52.164 --> 13:53.541
What kind of trick is this?

13:54.875 --> 13:56.418
It's not a trick at all.

14:03.968 --> 14:06.762
- [chimes]
- [computer] Seven minutes remain.

14:11.684 --> 14:12.560
[gasps]

14:12.643 --> 14:14.645
[wind whistling]

14:15.938 --> 14:17.940
[echoing clang]

14:24.655 --> 14:26.490
- [clanging]
- [screaming]

14:28.993 --> 14:30.995
[groaning]

14:32.746 --> 14:34.456
[panting]

14:35.291 --> 14:36.834
[yells]

14:38.586 --> 14:39.712
[yelling]

14:45.551 --> 14:47.803
[Arisu] What are you doing? Stop it!

14:47.887 --> 14:49.513
Getting the wristband off of me!

14:49.597 --> 14:50.681
[Arisu] Stop!

14:51.307 --> 14:52.725
[groans]

14:54.310 --> 14:56.562
[Tatta gasping] It's no use.

14:57.563 --> 14:59.023
I can't get it off.

15:01.358 --> 15:02.526
Pathetic.

15:04.445 --> 15:05.613
Arisu.

15:07.364 --> 15:08.240
You gotta do it.

15:09.950 --> 15:11.493
What do you mean, get it off?

15:12.578 --> 15:15.289
Well, I figured out a plan.

15:15.789 --> 15:17.583
There's 10,100 points here.

15:18.584 --> 15:22.338
If you hold onto it hidden in your pocket,
it'll be like there's two of us.

15:23.505 --> 15:25.424
Then our team might be able
to win that way.

15:27.092 --> 15:28.302
Tatta, I can't. No!

15:29.094 --> 15:31.847
They never said anything
about taking the wristband off.

15:32.598 --> 15:34.016
[breathing unsteadily]

15:34.099 --> 15:35.267
[Tatta groans]

15:36.060 --> 15:37.311
Please, Arisu!

15:38.228 --> 15:39.146
[yells]

15:39.730 --> 15:41.190
I don't think I can do it.

15:42.441 --> 15:43.817
Please, there's no time!

15:44.485 --> 15:45.694
Do it for me!

15:46.236 --> 15:47.780
[gasps and whimpers]

15:56.413 --> 15:58.123
We can win this way.

16:00.668 --> 16:03.170
[yelling]
Everybody's life is on the line here!

16:03.253 --> 16:04.254
What are you waiting for?

16:04.338 --> 16:06.840
- [PA chimes]
- [computer] Six minutes remain.

16:06.924 --> 16:08.175
[Tatta groans]

16:08.258 --> 16:09.385
Otherwise everyone will die!

16:12.221 --> 16:13.305
Arisu!

16:14.515 --> 16:15.349
Do it!

16:18.060 --> 16:20.771
You've just gotta do it, okay? Hurry!

16:21.563 --> 16:22.606
I can't.

16:23.565 --> 16:26.485
Please, or you'll kill everyone!
Do it for them!

16:28.237 --> 16:29.321
Just go!

16:30.489 --> 16:31.532
Do it!

16:34.076 --> 16:35.160
Arisu!

16:37.371 --> 16:38.706
Do it!

16:39.248 --> 16:40.499
[screams]

16:43.711 --> 16:45.713
[both gasping]

16:51.552 --> 16:53.721
[screaming]

16:54.680 --> 16:56.849
[gasping]

16:58.976 --> 17:01.645
[screaming]

17:01.729 --> 17:03.605
- [squelching]
- [panting]

17:07.401 --> 17:09.194
[Arisu hyperventilating]

17:09.278 --> 17:10.446
[groans]

17:10.529 --> 17:11.655
Tatta!

17:11.739 --> 17:12.906
[gasps] I'm sorry.

17:12.990 --> 17:14.366
I'm sorry!

17:14.950 --> 17:16.118
[weakly] No.

17:16.618 --> 17:18.162
I'm sorry I made you do it.

17:18.996 --> 17:20.080
I'm sure it was hard.

17:22.082 --> 17:23.333
[grunts]

17:24.334 --> 17:25.419
[groans]

17:27.421 --> 17:29.757
- Quick, take it.
- I've gotta stop the bleeding!

17:29.840 --> 17:31.258
Just take it!

17:39.725 --> 17:41.435
[gasping]

17:42.811 --> 17:43.896
Arisu.

17:45.481 --> 17:47.691
Remember when you thanked me earlier?

17:49.526 --> 17:51.236
I felt so much joy.

17:53.822 --> 17:54.990
It was like

17:55.866 --> 17:57.326
I was the hero for once.

17:59.953 --> 18:01.789
I promise I'll be fine.

18:01.872 --> 18:03.957
Don't worry, I'm not gonna die from this.

18:06.126 --> 18:08.587
Hurry up, or everyone else will die!

18:08.670 --> 18:10.297
- Go on!
- [sobbing]

18:12.716 --> 18:13.801
Go!

18:14.593 --> 18:15.427
Just go!

18:38.408 --> 18:40.327
[Kyuma] Whoa…

18:42.496 --> 18:45.707
You are way more screwed up
than I thought.

18:48.627 --> 18:50.504
I won the game, thanks to my friend.

18:52.047 --> 18:53.048
[sighs]

18:54.216 --> 18:57.636
Wow. I guess we finally lost the game.

19:02.141 --> 19:04.184
So even someone as wise as you

19:06.019 --> 19:07.729
is still afraid of death?

19:09.273 --> 19:10.357
[Kyuma] No.

19:11.900 --> 19:14.611
I'm thinking about my friend Shitara,
who died earlier.

19:18.699 --> 19:20.826
He said that if I let him die in vain,

19:22.202 --> 19:24.454
he'd beat the shit out of me
in the afterlife,

19:24.538 --> 19:25.873
and I know he meant it.

19:27.541 --> 19:30.169
And all my teammates
are gonna be disappointed in me.

19:34.965 --> 19:36.133
I'm sorry.

19:41.096 --> 19:42.806
You were the one who set the tone.

19:44.141 --> 19:47.394
We were all equals in this game,
and we gave everything.

19:48.437 --> 19:49.771
With all our hearts.

19:51.023 --> 19:53.525
I've never had this much passion
for anything.

19:56.361 --> 19:57.905
And you showed me how.

20:00.324 --> 20:01.491
Kyuma,

20:03.160 --> 20:05.787
you guys were a team before this,
weren't you?

20:11.501 --> 20:13.378
Kyuma, you asshole.

20:14.963 --> 20:17.341
I guess he dropped his guard
right at the end.

20:18.467 --> 20:19.384
[Maki scoffs]

20:20.219 --> 20:22.179
Well, aren't you the one to talk?

20:22.262 --> 20:23.805
[both laugh]

20:23.889 --> 20:25.599
Yeah, you're right.

20:26.767 --> 20:27.976
Without Kyuma,

20:28.852 --> 20:32.105
none of our sorry asses
would have made it this far in the game.

20:33.315 --> 20:35.651
We can't hold him responsible
for anything.

20:36.818 --> 20:37.945
That's right.

20:40.239 --> 20:41.615
Thanks, Kyuma.

20:43.242 --> 20:44.534
It was pretty fun.

20:47.329 --> 20:49.748
We'll do some more stupid shit
on the other side.

20:52.960 --> 20:54.211
[chuckles]

20:59.132 --> 21:01.093
- [laughs]
- [Arisu] Kyuma.

21:02.386 --> 21:05.889
You love your friends
as much as I love mine.

21:08.225 --> 21:11.561
And with every single game,
you kept on risking your lives.

21:13.021 --> 21:14.314
But you kept winning,

21:15.857 --> 21:17.150
and progressing more.

21:18.402 --> 21:20.279
We're all doing the same thing.

21:20.362 --> 21:23.365
Everyone just wants to stop
playing the game.

21:26.660 --> 21:27.869
Isn't that right?

21:33.542 --> 21:35.711
But it seems like,
even if you win them all,

21:36.545 --> 21:39.047
you still just become
citizens of Borderland.

21:39.131 --> 21:41.383
So do we get to go back
to where we came from?

21:44.803 --> 21:46.054
Tell me the truth.

21:48.390 --> 21:49.891
Do we get to go back?

21:56.773 --> 21:58.859
If that's what your intuition is saying,

22:00.360 --> 22:02.112
then maybe that's your truth.

22:08.410 --> 22:10.287
What kind of an answer is that?

22:14.750 --> 22:16.251
Come on, man.

22:25.302 --> 22:26.345
So there's…

22:28.221 --> 22:30.557
there's no point
in playing any of these games.

22:31.516 --> 22:33.935
Do you think you'll find out
if you stop playing?

22:38.690 --> 22:40.650
Well, what is it all supposed to mean?

22:46.907 --> 22:48.325
I don't think I can do it.

22:52.079 --> 22:54.539
I'm never gonna be as strong as you are.

22:56.083 --> 22:58.126
You'll never be like me, Arisu,

22:58.835 --> 23:00.253
and you shouldn't want that.

23:02.130 --> 23:03.715
You're playing your own game.

23:04.966 --> 23:06.718
You're the master of your own fate.

23:09.721 --> 23:10.597
[PA chimes]

23:11.181 --> 23:13.058
[computer] No time remains.

23:13.767 --> 23:19.356
It is game over for the King of Clubs
team, as they ended with fewer points.

23:19.856 --> 23:20.857
Arisu.

23:23.110 --> 23:24.277
Good luck to you.

23:32.911 --> 23:34.663
I don't want you to die!

23:38.083 --> 23:39.543
When we first met,

23:40.377 --> 23:42.587
we knew that one of us was going to die.

23:43.713 --> 23:45.966
If we hadn't met playing this game,
who's to say--

23:46.049 --> 23:48.468
The only reason we became this close

23:49.386 --> 23:51.304
was because we met playing the game.

23:54.474 --> 23:56.226
But if we had met somewhere else,

23:59.312 --> 24:01.773
then maybe we could have
actually been friends.

24:05.402 --> 24:07.696
We've been friends this whole time.

24:10.490 --> 24:11.366
Arisu.

24:13.452 --> 24:15.036
I hope you figure it out.

24:17.456 --> 24:19.040
How to live by your own rules.

24:20.041 --> 24:21.376
Your life is yours.

24:22.711 --> 24:24.463
Don't follow someone else's path.

24:35.849 --> 24:37.601
It was an honor playing with you.

24:52.908 --> 24:54.326
So this is the end.

24:56.453 --> 24:57.746
I had a great life.

25:02.667 --> 25:04.794
I lived it without a single regret.

25:09.633 --> 25:11.676
And I know that I'm ready to die.

25:33.490 --> 25:35.909
[sound of crowd cheering and whistling]

25:55.762 --> 25:57.097
Kyuma.

25:57.180 --> 25:58.974
[PA plays cheerful jingle]

25:59.474 --> 26:02.143
[computer] The player team wins.

26:02.227 --> 26:04.229
[rumbling]

26:52.819 --> 26:54.863
[Kuina] Usagi? Usagi!

26:57.949 --> 26:59.117
[gasps]

27:01.202 --> 27:02.329
Kuina.

27:02.954 --> 27:04.205
We won.

27:07.125 --> 27:08.585
What? Really?

27:11.838 --> 27:12.964
PLAYER TEAM
CONGRATULATIONS

27:13.048 --> 27:15.300
[Kuina] Arisu must have saved us somehow.

27:15.967 --> 27:17.177
[gasps]

27:19.220 --> 27:20.180
We won?

27:20.930 --> 27:21.890
[breathing shakily]

27:24.309 --> 27:26.478
[sobbing]

27:30.190 --> 27:31.733
[Arisu] Tatta, are you okay?

27:31.816 --> 27:32.942
Tatta!

27:33.443 --> 27:34.444
Hang on, Tatta!

27:40.116 --> 27:41.326
Just hang on.

27:44.204 --> 27:45.246
Tatta.

27:47.874 --> 27:49.334
[Tatta groaning weakly]

27:49.417 --> 27:50.502
[Arisu] Tatta.

27:51.419 --> 27:52.629
[Usagi gasps]

27:53.380 --> 27:54.214
[Arisu] Tatta,

27:55.298 --> 27:56.132
we won.

27:57.509 --> 27:58.551
We won,

27:59.469 --> 28:00.929
and it's all thanks to you.

28:02.597 --> 28:03.807
[Tatta] Sweet.

28:07.394 --> 28:09.479
[Arisu] Hey, come on, Tatta.

28:10.063 --> 28:11.481
Keep it together, all right?

28:12.273 --> 28:13.191
Tatta.

28:15.819 --> 28:16.945
You see?

28:18.822 --> 28:20.031
When I try,

28:21.032 --> 28:21.908
I can

28:23.118 --> 28:24.119
be great.

28:25.578 --> 28:27.956
[sobs] Yeah. You are great.

28:28.707 --> 28:30.291
We won because of you, Tatta.

28:33.503 --> 28:34.504
Thank you.

28:35.004 --> 28:37.006
[emotional music]

28:42.595 --> 28:44.347
Hey, Tatta!

28:45.598 --> 28:47.517
Tatta! Don't go!

28:48.977 --> 28:49.936
Don't you go!

28:50.520 --> 28:51.396
Tatta!

28:52.397 --> 28:53.523
[screams] Tatta!

28:53.606 --> 28:56.192
Oh no. Just hang on, Tatta!

28:56.776 --> 28:58.111
- [sighs]
- [Arisu] Tatta!

28:59.195 --> 29:00.488
Come on!

29:01.072 --> 29:02.240
Tatta!

29:03.450 --> 29:04.617
Tatta!

29:07.287 --> 29:08.538
[sobs] Tatta,

29:09.581 --> 29:10.999
don't leave me.

29:16.421 --> 29:18.006
[Arisu sobbing]

29:19.883 --> 29:21.885
[water lapping peacefully]

29:22.927 --> 29:24.929
[soft piano music]

29:46.785 --> 29:47.827
[Kuina sighs]

29:48.578 --> 29:49.788
It's a pretty view.

29:52.165 --> 29:54.125
This is a nice place to rest.

29:54.834 --> 29:55.919
[Usagi] Yeah.

30:04.135 --> 30:05.220
[sighs]

30:08.181 --> 30:09.390
We can't…

30:11.142 --> 30:13.394
let his death be for nothing.

30:15.647 --> 30:16.564
[sighs]

30:17.524 --> 30:19.192
We need to keep going,

30:20.109 --> 30:22.070
to keep Tatta's memory alive.

30:38.920 --> 30:41.172
I'm so fucking pissed off that I survived,

30:42.215 --> 30:43.758
and it's all because of you.

30:46.469 --> 30:47.345
Even so,

30:49.514 --> 30:51.683
I guess I'm grateful that I'm still alive.

30:54.102 --> 30:55.186
[sighs]

30:58.523 --> 30:59.816
So thank you.

31:17.458 --> 31:19.460
[ominous music]

31:32.515 --> 31:35.059
TEIO PRISON

32:13.514 --> 32:19.020
PUT ON A COLLAR AND GO UPSTAIRS
TO THE CENTRAL GUARDROOM

32:37.080 --> 32:38.206
[whirs]

32:38.289 --> 32:39.499
[chimes]

32:39.582 --> 32:40.917
[whirring]

32:42.126 --> 32:43.211
[chimes]

33:19.455 --> 33:20.790
[sighs]

33:22.000 --> 33:23.167
[PA chimes]

33:23.251 --> 33:25.795
[computer] Difficulty level,
Jack of Hearts.

33:28.006 --> 33:30.425
Game, Solitary Confinement.

33:31.426 --> 33:35.888
Rules. Guess the card suit
that appears on the back of your collar.

33:36.431 --> 33:40.268
However, you may not look
at the symbol yourself.

33:42.812 --> 33:44.647
I can't see anything.

33:45.231 --> 33:48.151
[computer] The time limit is
one hour per round.

33:48.234 --> 33:53.948
In the final five minutes,
enter your cell and disclose your symbol.

33:54.532 --> 33:56.117
[echoing thud]

33:57.201 --> 33:58.995
[lights buzzing]

34:11.215 --> 34:16.137
If you do not answer
with the correct symbol, it is game over.

34:16.220 --> 34:19.348
The collar will explode, and you will die.

34:19.432 --> 34:22.560
Additionally,
when the time limit reaches zero,

34:22.643 --> 34:26.439
the symbol on the collar will reset
and change for each round.

34:27.398 --> 34:31.861
Wait a sec. So that means we just have
to ask each other what our symbols are.

34:32.403 --> 34:33.696
That's easy, huh?

34:33.780 --> 34:35.323
I'm not so sure.

34:35.406 --> 34:38.409
They haven't told us
what the conditions to win are yet.

34:38.493 --> 34:40.286
[computer] The Solitary Confinement game

34:40.369 --> 34:43.498
is about how much
you can trust your fellow players.

34:43.581 --> 34:47.585
Be aware that your opponent,
the Jack of Hearts,

34:47.668 --> 34:50.254
has already been placed among you.

34:51.714 --> 34:53.007
Oh, that's good.

34:55.426 --> 34:56.844
[man] So one of us

34:58.054 --> 34:59.680
is the Jack of Hearts?

35:01.224 --> 35:02.475
[computer] How to win.

35:03.017 --> 35:05.478
Rounds repeat every hour.

35:05.561 --> 35:10.274
You win the game
when the Jack of Hearts dies.

35:11.442 --> 35:13.569
[grunting]

35:13.653 --> 35:15.738
[computer] Prohibited actions.

35:15.822 --> 35:19.408
Looking at your symbol
with a reflective surface is cheating.

35:20.034 --> 35:24.622
Players may not use weapons or violence
to kill fellow players.

35:25.623 --> 35:29.085
This means
that the only way this game will ever end

35:29.168 --> 35:32.088
is if the Jack gives the wrong answer.

35:32.964 --> 35:34.382
So, basically,

35:35.216 --> 35:38.928
no one here is getting out alive,
unless they lie to the Jack.

35:39.011 --> 35:41.764
[computer] There is no limit
to the number of rounds.

35:41.848 --> 35:43.224
There's no limit?

35:43.766 --> 35:46.686
[computer] Enough food has been provided.

35:48.271 --> 35:49.230
What?

35:58.197 --> 36:00.241
[computer]
While participating in this game,

36:00.324 --> 36:03.536
no days will be removed from your visas.

36:05.288 --> 36:07.290
So we need to start lying,

36:07.373 --> 36:10.126
find the Jack of Hearts,
and kill them off,

36:10.209 --> 36:12.879
or we'll live out the rest of our days
in this prison.

36:15.798 --> 36:17.633
Solitary for life.

36:18.551 --> 36:20.845
[computer] The game will now commence.

36:21.387 --> 36:22.471
ROUND ONE

36:22.555 --> 36:26.100
You can roam freely
until it is time to enter your cell.

36:34.734 --> 36:36.277
Is this for real?

36:41.616 --> 36:42.450
[man] Hey, man.

36:43.868 --> 36:46.454
Would you mind telling me
what my symbol is?

36:46.537 --> 36:48.039
And then I can tell you yours.

36:48.581 --> 36:49.540
Okay.

36:50.041 --> 36:53.544
So, the 20 of us
need to eliminate each other

36:53.628 --> 36:57.256
until we somehow figure out
who the Jack of Hearts is.

36:59.342 --> 37:01.719
What makes you think
that anyone is trustworthy?

37:05.723 --> 37:07.391
Do you wanna go downstairs?

37:20.112 --> 37:21.155
[scoffs]

37:25.576 --> 37:26.911
[woman 1] I have an idea.

37:26.994 --> 37:30.206
How about we get together
and make teams to tell each other?

37:30.289 --> 37:33.000
So that way, nobody can lie.

37:33.084 --> 37:34.168
[woman 2] Good idea.

37:34.252 --> 37:37.004
Um, would you mind
if I joined up with you?

37:37.088 --> 37:38.339
[woman 3] Me too?

37:38.422 --> 37:40.633
Excuse me. I'd like to join as well.

37:40.716 --> 37:43.594
[laughs] Sure! The more the merrier!

37:43.678 --> 37:44.845
Can I join too, please?

37:44.929 --> 37:47.556
Hey. I want you to tell me
what my symbol is.

37:47.640 --> 37:48.849
[man] Um… Okay.

37:49.684 --> 37:51.936
Tell me what my symbol is, man.

37:52.853 --> 37:54.063
Go on.

37:54.146 --> 37:55.189
- Uh…
- Huh?

37:56.065 --> 37:58.734
Why, can't you tell me?
Then I'll look at yours.

37:59.318 --> 38:00.194
Huh?

38:01.445 --> 38:02.321
[chuckles]

38:03.155 --> 38:04.907
Okay, now tell me mine.

38:04.991 --> 38:06.701
- [man 1] All right.
- [man 2] Come on.

38:06.784 --> 38:08.869
Hey, wanna tell each other the answer?

38:10.371 --> 38:12.290
If you're trying to survive,

38:12.373 --> 38:15.334
I would examine all the people here
a little more carefully.

38:16.752 --> 38:19.714
Make sure you keep
the ones who don't lie close.

38:21.674 --> 38:24.135
For all you know,
I'm the one who might be the Jack.

38:26.762 --> 38:27.805
You see?

38:28.306 --> 38:30.433
They all started breaking off into groups.

38:30.975 --> 38:34.437
Everyone wants to know
who's trustworthy and who's not.

38:38.357 --> 38:39.358
Take those two.

38:41.068 --> 38:42.111
[man 3] Listen.

38:42.903 --> 38:44.238
If you wanna be safe…

38:44.322 --> 38:47.325
Before the game started,
you wanna know what they were doing?

38:48.701 --> 38:50.077
[woman whimpering]

38:51.329 --> 38:53.164
[sobbing and groaning]

38:57.918 --> 38:59.003
What?

38:59.962 --> 39:03.674
That guy wants to control everything
she does to exert power over her

39:04.675 --> 39:08.012
so that she can't interact
with any of the other players.

39:09.388 --> 39:11.432
Which is smart, in the long run.

39:11.515 --> 39:14.060
If you've got someone
you can trust that much,

39:14.143 --> 39:15.811
that's how you can win the game.

39:15.895 --> 39:16.771
[man 4] Hey.

39:20.441 --> 39:23.277
- Doesn't look like you have a partner yet.
- [man 5] Hearts…

39:23.361 --> 39:25.696
[man 4] Tell me what my symbol is,
and I'll tell you yours.

39:25.780 --> 39:27.656
- [woman] I don't know.
- [man 5] Spades.

39:28.491 --> 39:29.825
[woman 2] Clubs.

39:30.826 --> 39:33.120
That's a pretty aggressive
attitude to take.

39:33.954 --> 39:34.789
[man 4] Huh?

39:35.790 --> 39:38.793
That kind of childishness
makes you painfully transparent.

39:40.461 --> 39:44.256
You're ashamed of the darkness inside you,
which makes you petty and jealous.

39:44.340 --> 39:47.301
You try to keep yourself safe
behind those bangs.

39:48.302 --> 39:51.764
You hide your face so that
people won't see your ugly, empty soul.

39:53.557 --> 39:58.062
You're a pathetic excuse of a human being
who judges others to feel better.

40:02.358 --> 40:03.567
Pathetic and small.

40:04.193 --> 40:06.028
But that's what I like about you.

40:14.120 --> 40:15.830
We should be friends.

40:27.716 --> 40:28.968
Hey.

40:29.051 --> 40:30.928
Do you wanna join our team?

40:32.430 --> 40:34.181
No pressure or anything.

40:34.765 --> 40:36.267
It's not that I don't want to.

40:36.976 --> 40:39.770
Okay. We'll join the group.

40:41.939 --> 40:43.732
- Do you wanna join us?
- Yes.

40:43.816 --> 40:45.317
Welcome to the group. Welcome.

40:47.611 --> 40:49.530
So I'm gonna go first, okay?

40:50.114 --> 40:52.616
I hope you'll all give me
the right answer.

40:53.534 --> 40:55.828
Oh, Urumi, yours is…

40:55.911 --> 40:56.954
is a heart.

40:57.037 --> 40:58.205
- Heart.
- [all] Heart. Heart.

40:58.289 --> 40:59.206
- Heart. Yes.
- Yeah.

41:00.875 --> 41:04.295
Okay, will you please do mine next?

41:04.378 --> 41:05.421
Yours is a heart too.

41:05.504 --> 41:06.881
- Heart, yes.
- Heart.

41:06.964 --> 41:08.257
Heart.

41:08.340 --> 41:10.217
- Mm-hmm.
- I'll go next.

41:12.678 --> 41:14.263
- You're a spade.
- [all] Yes. Spade.

41:14.346 --> 41:15.848
- It's a spade.
- See, it's a spade.

41:15.931 --> 41:18.142
- [man] Uh, may I go next?
- [all] Sure. Yeah.

41:18.726 --> 41:19.685
- Diamond.
- [man] Diamond?

41:19.768 --> 41:21.395
- [all] Yes, yes, diamond.
- It's a diamond.

41:21.479 --> 41:22.605
Yes, a diamond.

41:23.981 --> 41:25.733
[all] Yes. Diamond. Diamond.

41:25.816 --> 41:26.775
- That's it.
- Mm-hmm.

41:28.277 --> 41:29.612
- Club.
- You're a club. That's it.

41:29.695 --> 41:31.447
- A club, yes. It's a club.
- Club, yes.

41:31.989 --> 41:33.407
[man 2] Oh, okay, I'll go next.

41:33.491 --> 41:34.450
[buzzer sounds]

41:34.533 --> 41:37.328
[computer] It is time to give your answer.

41:37.411 --> 41:42.124
Please enter a solitary confinement cell
of your choosing.

41:52.092 --> 41:53.260
[whirring]

41:55.554 --> 41:56.931
[clanking]

41:57.014 --> 41:58.182
[buzzing]

41:58.265 --> 42:00.518
[computer] Please give your answer.

42:02.061 --> 42:03.020
Diamond.

42:12.863 --> 42:14.073
[bell rings]

42:14.156 --> 42:16.158
- [horn sounds]
- [lock clanks]

42:28.796 --> 42:29.797
[Urumi] Wow.

42:30.631 --> 42:32.383
That was so easy.

42:32.466 --> 42:33.634
[laughs]

42:39.682 --> 42:42.768
- [woman 1] Ah, thank goodness!
- [woman 2] Let's do this every round.

42:42.851 --> 42:43.936
[woman 1] Yes.

42:44.395 --> 42:46.480
[woman 2] Oh my gosh. I'm so relieved.

42:46.564 --> 42:47.815
[woman 1] Thank goodness.

42:47.898 --> 42:49.233
[alarm blares]

42:49.316 --> 42:51.860
[computer] Round two begins now.

42:53.070 --> 42:54.029
[chimes]

42:55.573 --> 42:56.907
[Urumi sighs]

42:58.325 --> 43:00.828
- Thank you so much. Let's do that again.
- Yes, thank you so much.

43:00.911 --> 43:04.331
- Yes, thank you. Thank you so much.
- Yes, thank you.

43:04.415 --> 43:05.624
- Thank you so much.
- Thank you.

43:05.708 --> 43:09.044
- [yells] An answer!
- Thanks everyone, for being honest.

43:09.128 --> 43:10.379
I feel very relieved.

43:10.462 --> 43:13.841
I keep wondering
how long this is going to go on for.

43:15.175 --> 43:17.720
Either the Jack will start to kill,

43:17.803 --> 43:20.889
or someone who's afraid of the Jack
will start to kill.

43:20.973 --> 43:21.974
[man] …stick together…

43:22.057 --> 43:26.145
Until either or both of those things
happen, this will never end.

43:26.228 --> 43:27.813
Exactly.

43:29.481 --> 43:33.277
[gasps] As long as we keep being honest
with each other, we'll be all right.

43:34.403 --> 43:35.446
Or not.

43:36.238 --> 43:37.531
[angry man] What the fuck?

43:37.615 --> 43:38.449
[whimpers]

43:39.783 --> 43:42.828
- [sobs]
- I told you to give me the answer!

43:44.079 --> 43:46.248
[breathing shakily]

43:48.334 --> 43:49.668
- [angry man yells]
- You all right?

43:49.752 --> 43:50.753
[gasps]

43:53.172 --> 43:54.673
- Tell him he's a club.
- [gasps]

44:03.891 --> 44:05.976
[angry man] Looks to me
like you want another beating.

44:06.060 --> 44:07.728
- Huh?
- [groaning]

44:08.520 --> 44:10.064
- [growls] Huh?
- [whimpers]

44:10.147 --> 44:11.023
Huh?

44:11.106 --> 44:13.067
- [punch lands]
- [victim groans and sobs]

44:15.402 --> 44:16.654
Give me the answer!

44:17.488 --> 44:19.156
C-- Club.

44:19.239 --> 44:21.659
- Huh?
- [whimpers] Club!

44:27.706 --> 44:29.041
[laughs]

44:30.668 --> 44:32.628
Don't wait so long next time.

44:32.711 --> 44:33.796
[groans]

44:45.516 --> 44:46.767
- [gasps]
- Shh!

44:48.519 --> 44:50.688
Now the game is really starting.

45:07.996 --> 45:09.456
Are you all right?

45:10.999 --> 45:11.875
Yeah.

45:12.543 --> 45:15.295
How would you like to join up
with our group instead?

45:18.757 --> 45:19.842
Thank you.

45:32.104 --> 45:35.107
[computer] It is time to give your answer.

45:35.190 --> 45:39.528
Please enter a solitary confinement cell
of your choosing.

45:58.922 --> 45:59.965
[buzzer sounds]

46:00.048 --> 46:02.342
[computer] Please give your answer.

46:02.968 --> 46:03.969
[inhales]

46:04.052 --> 46:05.387
The answer's club.

46:18.150 --> 46:19.109
GENKI KIRIU

46:19.193 --> 46:20.235
[buzzer sounds]

46:21.153 --> 46:22.863
[woman 1] Oh, I can't believe it.

46:22.946 --> 46:24.156
[man] I know him.

46:24.740 --> 46:26.492
- [woman 2] I'm so scared.
- [man] That bully.

46:27.451 --> 46:30.412
- [woman 1] I wonder who's gonna be next.
- [man] Okay, great.

46:31.371 --> 46:34.541
- [woman 1] Do you think it could be me?
- [woman 2] What? I don't get it.

46:34.625 --> 46:35.834
[woman 1] I don't know.

46:35.918 --> 46:37.503
[man] He hit that guy.

46:37.586 --> 46:39.546
Lo-- look. Someone's missing.

46:40.047 --> 46:42.049
- [woman 3] That big dumb guy, right?
- Is that right?

46:42.132 --> 46:43.467
Yes, yes, it was him, yes.

46:44.051 --> 46:46.220
- [woman] Remember, we're a team.
- [man] Yeah.

46:47.721 --> 46:49.431
[woman] If we keep
telling the truth, then…

46:49.515 --> 46:51.099
- [man] It was me.
- …everyone will be okay.

46:51.183 --> 46:52.142
Hey.

46:52.226 --> 46:54.102
[man] …what his suit was, that's all…

46:54.186 --> 46:56.647
[Urumi] That guy must be the Jack.

46:57.606 --> 46:58.482
[woman] Yeah, I know.

46:58.565 --> 47:02.277
- He lied to that big bully and killed him.
- [man] Someone has to…

47:03.153 --> 47:05.697
- Okay, we stay together.
- [woman] I don't know who to trust.

47:05.781 --> 47:09.034
I think we'd better kill him next turn.

47:09.117 --> 47:10.786
- [woman] What do you think?
- What?

47:12.412 --> 47:14.206
- [man] You tell me…
- Are you saying…

47:14.289 --> 47:17.751
- [man] …trust each other…
- …we should lie to him?

47:17.835 --> 47:19.920
- [woman] How are we supposed to know?
- [man] What…

47:20.003 --> 47:21.296
Of course.

47:21.880 --> 47:24.049
He's definitely the Jack.

47:24.550 --> 47:26.510
And if not, he's still dangerous.

47:27.177 --> 47:30.097
We should eliminate him
while we have the chance.

47:39.147 --> 47:40.399
[gasps]

47:54.121 --> 47:55.747
[man 1] Next up is, uh…

47:55.831 --> 47:57.165
[Urumi] You!

47:57.249 --> 47:59.084
- [groaning]
- [man 2] Okay, great.

47:59.167 --> 48:00.836
- [whimpering]
- [man 3] Oh, you're a heart.

48:00.919 --> 48:02.379
- Yeah, a heart.
- [woman 1] Yes. Heart.

48:02.462 --> 48:04.339
- Yes, that's a heart.
- [all] Heart. Heart.

48:04.923 --> 48:07.301
- [woman 2] May I go next?
- [man 1] Yes, yes, please.

48:08.927 --> 48:10.387
Your symbol is a diamond.

48:11.388 --> 48:12.890
- [woman 3] Diamond, yes.
- [all] Diamond.

48:12.973 --> 48:14.725
- That's a diamond.
- It's a diamond.

48:15.475 --> 48:16.810
Can you do mine next?

48:18.687 --> 48:21.481
Looks like your symbol's a spade.

48:22.941 --> 48:24.276
- Uh, yes.
- Mm-hmm.

48:24.359 --> 48:25.527
- [all] Spade. Spade.
- Yes.

48:25.611 --> 48:26.820
- It's a spade.
- Spade.

48:26.904 --> 48:29.072
- Spade.
- Thank you very much.

48:35.162 --> 48:36.204
- Uh…
- Hm…

48:39.583 --> 48:40.792
Uh…

48:53.305 --> 48:54.431
[loud crunch]

48:58.602 --> 48:59.937
[buzzer sounds]

49:00.020 --> 49:02.397
[computer] Please give your answer.

49:02.481 --> 49:03.857
[trembling]

49:04.691 --> 49:05.859
It's a spade.

49:08.153 --> 49:09.571
[explosion echoes]

49:09.655 --> 49:10.530
AKIFUMI SETO

49:10.614 --> 49:11.698
[buzzer sounds]

49:14.117 --> 49:17.371
- [alarm blares]
- [computer] Round four begins now.

49:17.955 --> 49:19.873
[woman 1] What? I don't get it.

49:20.832 --> 49:23.293
[woman 2] I guess that guy
wasn't the Jack of Hearts.

49:24.461 --> 49:26.046
[sighing nervously]

49:27.172 --> 49:28.799
See? Told you this would happen.

49:30.467 --> 49:32.302
People are starting to get nervous.

49:32.386 --> 49:34.471
I know they said there was no time limit…

49:36.181 --> 49:38.976
except that people
are actually starting to die now.

49:40.185 --> 49:42.270
I'm not sure we'll find the Jack at all.

50:06.878 --> 50:08.171
[breathing shakily]

50:16.596 --> 50:17.973
That girl there,

50:18.056 --> 50:21.935
she wasn't on our side when we tried
to get our stories straight earlier.

50:23.311 --> 50:25.188
Should we kill her? Hmm?

50:37.200 --> 50:38.577
[man] Please, do mine.

50:40.120 --> 50:41.288
Oh, uh… Diamond.

50:41.371 --> 50:44.416
- [all] Yes. Diamond.
- [all] Diamond. Diamond. It is.

50:46.835 --> 50:49.421
All right, will you do mine next, please?

50:53.091 --> 50:55.052
It looks like your symbol is

50:55.635 --> 50:56.845
a club!

50:56.928 --> 50:58.597
- [laughs]
- [man] Yes, yes.

50:58.680 --> 51:00.766
- It's club.
- Club.

51:00.849 --> 51:02.684
- Yes, club. Club, it is.
- Yes.

51:02.768 --> 51:04.603
- It's a club.
- [gasps]

51:05.979 --> 51:07.522
Thank you very much.

51:13.904 --> 51:15.155
[buzzer sounds]

51:15.238 --> 51:17.574
[computer] Please give your answer.

51:19.409 --> 51:20.494
[gasps]

51:21.369 --> 51:22.370
Spade.

51:23.872 --> 51:25.749
[explosion echoes]

51:30.378 --> 51:31.630
MEISA TOKUI

51:31.713 --> 51:32.923
[clank]

51:33.006 --> 51:35.300
[lively cello music]

51:35.383 --> 51:37.969
- [woman 1] You're a spade.
- [all] Spade. Spade.

51:38.053 --> 51:39.471
[woman 2] Thank you so much.

51:40.305 --> 51:41.890
[woman 3] Do mine next, please.

51:42.557 --> 51:44.142
- [Urumi] It's a club.
- [man 1] Oh yeah.

51:44.226 --> 51:46.144
- [man 2] Yes, it's a club.
- [all] Club. Club.

51:46.228 --> 51:48.522
- Mm-hmm.
- [woman whispers] What do you think she…

51:49.731 --> 51:51.650
[Urumi] Your symbol is

51:51.733 --> 51:53.151
a heart!

51:53.235 --> 51:54.361
- Heart, yes.
- [man 3] Mm-hm.

51:54.444 --> 51:56.363
- Yes. Heart.
- [woman] Heart it is, yes.

51:56.446 --> 51:58.448
Will you do mine now?

52:03.286 --> 52:04.788
You're a spade.

52:04.871 --> 52:06.873
- [man] Yes.
- [all] Spade. Spade.

52:06.957 --> 52:09.126
- [man] Yes, spade.
- Thank you.

52:14.172 --> 52:15.006
[woman] Um,

52:16.341 --> 52:17.259
excuse me.

52:18.593 --> 52:19.845
Excuse me.

52:21.972 --> 52:23.265
Would you mind

52:23.765 --> 52:25.976
telling me what my symbol is, please?

52:28.520 --> 52:30.689
I don't think my group is being honest.

52:34.484 --> 52:35.443
Okay.

52:35.944 --> 52:38.196
[gasps] Thank you very much.

52:39.406 --> 52:40.448
Here.

52:46.288 --> 52:47.455
It's a club.

52:48.623 --> 52:49.583
[woman] Club?

52:51.418 --> 52:52.377
Club!

52:54.546 --> 52:55.630
Club!

52:56.882 --> 52:59.885
Thank you very much. Thank you very much!

53:00.385 --> 53:02.053
Club. [chuckles]

53:02.929 --> 53:04.306
[laughing]

53:07.142 --> 53:08.560
Can't be too careful, right?

53:14.316 --> 53:16.693
[laughing]

53:20.697 --> 53:21.615
[buzzer sounds]

53:21.698 --> 53:23.992
[computer] Please give your answer.

53:27.996 --> 53:29.080
Club.

53:30.207 --> 53:31.750
[giggles]

53:37.422 --> 53:39.049
[explosion echoes]

53:39.132 --> 53:40.133
SHINOBU FURUTA

53:40.217 --> 53:41.176
[clank]

53:41.259 --> 53:44.471
- [alarm blares]
- [computer] Round six begins now.

53:44.554 --> 53:46.556
[breathing shakily]

53:49.351 --> 53:51.102
Why are they all tricking each other?

53:52.103 --> 53:53.980
Wow, are you really surprised?

53:54.981 --> 53:57.234
Nobody wants to be the next to die.

53:58.735 --> 54:00.320
[trembling]

54:06.660 --> 54:08.662
[breathing unsteadily]

54:13.291 --> 54:15.043
[trembling]

54:17.921 --> 54:19.464
[whimpering]

54:22.467 --> 54:23.635
[explosion echoes]

54:23.718 --> 54:24.844
[clank]

54:25.595 --> 54:28.306
- [alarm blares]
- [computer] Round nine begins now.

54:29.975 --> 54:31.059
I can't…

54:31.142 --> 54:32.602
I can't take it.

54:33.311 --> 54:34.562
I'm gonna throw up.

54:34.646 --> 54:35.855
[retches]

54:35.939 --> 54:37.816
- [groans]
- [Urumi] Keep it together!

54:38.316 --> 54:40.944
- [moaning and retching]
- [Urumi] You're a club.

54:41.027 --> 54:43.196
Okay, you tell me mine.

54:43.280 --> 54:44.281
[panting]

54:45.573 --> 54:46.574
Uh, diam--

54:48.159 --> 54:49.494
Uh…

54:49.577 --> 54:51.246
Dia… [gasps]

54:52.038 --> 54:53.248
You're a heart.

54:53.331 --> 54:54.582
[panting]

54:54.666 --> 54:55.583
Heart.

54:55.667 --> 54:57.210
- It's a heart.
- Heart.

55:00.839 --> 55:02.215
[groaning softly]

55:04.092 --> 55:05.260
[coughing]

55:14.477 --> 55:16.521
Let's eliminate him now.

55:17.063 --> 55:18.398
- Huh?
- Huh?

55:18.481 --> 55:20.900
He was thinking about tricking me.

55:21.860 --> 55:24.487
It seems he has a problem with how I work.

55:24.571 --> 55:25.572
But…

55:26.197 --> 55:29.743
If we don't get rid of him right away,
we'll all be in danger.

55:33.538 --> 55:36.207
- [alarm blares]
- [computer] Round nine is almost over.

55:36.791 --> 55:40.503
[anxious man] I think we should
eliminate her, now.

55:42.380 --> 55:43.798
[both gasp]

55:43.882 --> 55:45.967
We're all in danger because of her.

55:46.843 --> 55:49.763
We can't keep letting that psycho

55:50.347 --> 55:52.515
do whatever she wants to us.

55:52.599 --> 55:54.601
[all breathing shakily]

56:03.693 --> 56:05.403
[sniffling]

56:08.490 --> 56:10.492
- This, uh… This is for you.
- Oh.

56:10.575 --> 56:11.868
Um, here's something to drink.

56:11.951 --> 56:13.453
[Urumi] What else did you bring me?

56:13.536 --> 56:15.372
[anxious man] And some crackers too.

56:17.415 --> 56:19.459
[Urumi] Oh, you have no taste.

56:19.542 --> 56:22.045
[anxious man] I have cookies.
Would you like a cookie?

56:22.128 --> 56:23.588
[Urumi] I hate cookies.

56:23.671 --> 56:25.673
I think we should kill them both.

56:25.757 --> 56:27.008
[Urumi] I hate chocolate.

56:27.092 --> 56:28.343
What do you say?

56:28.426 --> 56:30.804
- [anxious man] What else would you like?
- [gasps]

56:40.480 --> 56:42.065
[both sobbing]

56:56.663 --> 56:58.498
You're a spade.

56:59.874 --> 57:00.959
Diamond.

57:02.794 --> 57:03.878
Diamond.

57:04.462 --> 57:05.713
It's spade.

57:06.714 --> 57:07.799
Diamond.

57:09.259 --> 57:10.427
Thanks, guys.

57:10.510 --> 57:13.012
You're the only people I can trust now!

57:19.144 --> 57:20.895
[breathing shakily]

57:20.979 --> 57:23.189
[computer] Please give your answer.

57:28.361 --> 57:29.320
Diamond.

57:29.404 --> 57:30.530
Spade!

57:40.457 --> 57:41.666
URUMI AKAMAKI

57:41.749 --> 57:42.584
MOTOHIKO KANEKO

57:51.968 --> 57:53.136
Spade.

57:55.263 --> 57:56.347
Club.

58:02.645 --> 58:04.397
[explosion echoes]

58:05.648 --> 58:08.693
[man in suit] They all fell
for the Jack of Hearts' trap.

58:10.820 --> 58:14.073
Once team members start killing
each other, the trust is broken,

58:14.157 --> 58:15.909
and the group is destroyed.

58:18.495 --> 58:20.872
Well, I don't think
that we have that problem.

58:21.456 --> 58:22.373
Right.

58:23.708 --> 58:25.585
You don't need to worry about that.

58:26.503 --> 58:28.087
Not while I'm protecting you.

58:31.341 --> 58:32.926
Thank you, master.

58:37.931 --> 58:39.182
[breathing shakily]

58:41.893 --> 58:42.977
[sobs]

58:46.314 --> 58:48.566
I don't think I can keep
playing this game.

58:51.194 --> 58:52.278
Diamond.

58:52.862 --> 58:54.864
[sobbing]

58:59.536 --> 59:00.995
How much longer, man?

59:07.794 --> 59:09.504
It's so messed up.

59:14.717 --> 59:15.843
I thought that…

59:17.595 --> 59:19.514
people were much better than this.

59:22.392 --> 59:24.269
Man, you led a charmed life.

59:25.687 --> 59:26.771
[sobs]

59:27.355 --> 59:28.439
I'm sorry.

59:29.691 --> 59:31.568
But this is our reality now.

59:32.360 --> 59:34.320
Maybe we won't get out of this alive.

59:35.905 --> 59:40.410
But even so, all we can do for now
is help each other

59:41.703 --> 59:43.705
so that we can get out of this game.

59:48.251 --> 59:49.335
[sniffles]

59:50.253 --> 59:51.087
Okay?

59:51.713 --> 59:53.006
We can do this.

59:58.094 --> 59:59.137
Okay.

01:00:00.805 --> 01:00:02.056
What's my symbol?

01:00:03.933 --> 01:00:05.476
[trembling]

01:00:11.941 --> 01:00:12.984
Heart.

01:00:31.544 --> 01:00:32.670
I can't do it.

01:00:38.092 --> 01:00:39.135
I can't.

01:00:40.887 --> 01:00:42.263
I can't do this.

01:00:42.347 --> 01:00:45.933
- [buzzer sounds]
- [computer] Please give your answer.

01:00:55.652 --> 01:00:56.944
[gasps]

01:00:58.946 --> 01:01:00.490
I won't do this.

01:01:05.995 --> 01:01:07.038
IPPEI OKI

01:01:17.340 --> 01:01:18.466
[sighs]

01:01:18.549 --> 01:01:21.969
You were too kind for this world, Ippei.

01:01:27.058 --> 01:01:28.685
Well, that's settled.

01:01:29.727 --> 01:01:31.521
Seems I've lost my partner.

01:01:49.664 --> 01:01:51.749
Looks like I'm screwed. [sighs]

01:01:53.167 --> 01:01:54.752
[theme music]
